I have never had this happen.  Maybe NetHack is writing over some system
information.  Has this happened to anyone else?

>Symptom#2
>   After I ran another program _after_ running Nethack, I got the message:
>
>"A Nymph just stole your .EXE file"
>I searched the NETHACK.EXE file for this text, and found it, as well as some
>other text about a dog stealing memory or something like that.

This text comes from the overlay manager.  Aparently it was designed
especially for NetHack, and the designers made the error messages with a
NetHack-like flavor.  This message means that the overlay manager is trying
to find nethack.exe to load in another overlay.  I have no idea why it is
doing this, though.  (Don't look at me, I only compile here :-)  If anyone
else experiences these problems (or any others) please send me mail.

>I scanned nethack.exe for any known viruses, but there was none.
>
>Anybody have any ideas about this??
>

I regularly check my system with the latest version of SCANV so it is NOT
a virus.  I will see if I can reproduce this behavior.  Suggestions or
problems can be mailed to the address below.

